// Next fit: the search starts at the rover, the block the last allocation or
// free touched, and wraps to the first block only if nothing past it fits. A
// first-fit walk from the start crossed every block ever handed out for each
// request; this one almost always stops on the first or second. When the wrap
// finds nothing either, the heap grows by an island.
find_fit(word need) {
  word hrv = peek64((import crt_heap));
  word r = fit_from(hrv, need, 0);
  word w = fit_wrap(r, hrv, need);
} return word w;
